  "title": "Motion Machine: written, not edited",
  "language": "en",
  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "f1",
      "text": "A piece is a story (story.json) worn by a style (style.json); the kit draws every frame from t alone. There is no timeline to edit.",
      "source": "SPEC.md §1-§2; skill/motion-machine/SKILL.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2",
      "text": "The same story renders as a film and as a clicker deck. This film ships in 16x9 and 9x16; pieces/demo-deck tells the same story in presses.",
      "source": "SPEC.md §1, §10; pieces/demo-film/story.json formats"
    },
    {
      "id": "f3",
      "text": "pieces/demo-swap-editorial, demo-swap-kinetic and demo-swap-calm-product are one story (only id differs) in the three shipped presets: editorial = paper x calm, kinetic = signal x kinetic, calm-product = linen x premium. The tiles are their frames at the rest of scene 2.",
      "source": "styles/presets/*.json field from; pieces/demo-swap-*/story.json; capture/assets.json swap-*"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4",
      "text": "The phone and laptop show pieces/golden-film-editorial at its first rest (the poster instant, 1.033 s) rendered in 9x16 and in 16x9 from the one story.",
      "source": "pieces/golden-film-editorial/story.json formats; capture/assets.json golden-editorial-*"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5",
      "text": "mm brand capture on fixtures/capture/site/index.html (the fictional Harbour & Pine) read seven colour roles; accent #D2491F, the most saturated colour on buttons, links and headings.",
      "source": "pieces/demo-film/capture/harbour-pine.json; harbour-pine.capture-notes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "f6",
      "text": "Capture warned that Harbour & Pine's muted #6A7478 on canvas #F6F1E7 is 4.26:1, below the 4.5:1 W-CONTRAST asks of video text; it was darkened to #636C70 (4.77:1) before the skill was made.",
      "source": "pieces/demo-film/capture/harbour-pine.capture-notes.md; harbour-pine-fixed.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7",
      "text": "mm motion capture on pieces/golden-film-kinetic/out/golden-film-kinetic-16x9.mp4 read 900 frames and found 7 cuts, 18 arrivals, energy high.",
      "source": "pieces/demo-film/capture/kinetic-ref.capture-notes.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "f8",
      "text": "mm skill new --brand harbour-pine-fixed.json wrote the skill harbour-pine-motion: SKILL.md, style/ (brand, motion, style), fonts/ with licences, facts.md; 21 files.",
      "source": "pieces/demo-film/capture/harbour-pine-skill/"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9",
      "text": "pieces/golden-film-kinetic is 30 s at 30 fps: 900 frames, each drawn from t alone; mm export --prove rendered every one a second time in a fresh page and found them byte-identical. The sheet shows one frame a second, t = 0.5 to 29.5 s.",
      "source": "pieces/golden-film-kinetic/out/export.json; SPEC.md §2; capture/assets.json contact-golden-kinetic"
    },
    {
      "id": "f10",
      "text": "The gate checks 40 rules: 14 errors (G-) and 26 warnings (W-). On pieces/golden-film-kinetic: 34 PASS, 1 WARN, 5 SKIP.",
      "source": "SPEC.md §7; scripts/check/ (14 G-*.mjs, 26 W-*.mjs); pieces/golden-film-kinetic/out/check.json"
    },
    {
      "id": "f11",
      "text": "120 patterns in 12 groups: 3d 3, data 10, devices 5, emphasis 8, entrances 18, exits 4, layouts 15, moves 12, screen 8, sound 9, text 10, transitions 18. None carries a brand. The wall shows each one's demo still in this film's style.",
      "source": "node scripts/mm.mjs pattern list; node scripts/pattern-lint.mjs; capture/assets.json library-wall"
    },
    {
      "id": "f12",
      "text": "mm sound places synthesised cues on the beats and mixes to the style's loudness target, -14 LUFS.",
      "source": "styles/motion/kinetic.json sound.loudnessLufs; references/sound.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "f13",
      "text": "Motion Machine is licensed Apache-2.0.",
      "source": "README.md Status; LICENSE"
    }
  ],
